       <code>employee.letters.view</code>. Tenant isolation is structural here and always has been; this is the
       second lock &mdash; which rows, not which screen &mdash; and until recently there was no
       such lock at all.</p>
  </div>

<?php elseif ($route === 'letters'): ?>
<?php
    $employeeId = (string) ($_GET['e'] ?? '');
    $templateKey = (string) ($_GET['t'] ?? '');
    $toAll = $employeeId === 'all';
    $subject = $employeeId === '' || $toAll ? null : $store->find('employees', $employeeId);
    // BLANK = THE EMPLOYEE'S OWN SALARY-STRUCTURE EFFECTIVE DATE (owner, 15 Oct) — joining, end of unpaid
    // training, latest appraisal or confirmation; for "all employees", each person's own.
    $effTyped = trim((string) ($_GET['eff'] ?? '')) === '' ? '' : letterEffectiveDate((string) $_GET['eff']);
    $effective = $effTyped !== '' ? $effTyped : ($subject !== null ? (string) (letterContextFor(null, orgEnrich($store, $subject), '', $company)['effective_date']) : '');
    $template = $templateKey === '' ? null : $letters->find($templateKey);
    $preview = $subject !== null && $template !== null
        ? $letters->render($template, orgEnrich($store, $subject), letterContextFor($template, orgEnrich($store, $subject), (string) ($_GET['eff'] ?? ''), $company))
        : null;
    // ALL EMPLOYEES: every active employee in view rendered the same way; who
    // is ready and who is refused (and why) is shown BEFORE anything is issued.
    $bulk = null;

    if ($toAll && $template !== null) {
        $bulk = ['ready' => [], 'refused' => []];

        foreach (letterRecipients($store, $scope, $may('employee.letters.view')) as $one) {
            $r = $letters->render($template, orgEnrich($store, $one), letterContextFor($template, orgEnrich($store, $one), (string) ($_GET['eff'] ?? ''), $company));
            $r['ok'] ? $bulk['ready'][] = ['e' => $one, 'body' => $r['body']] : $bulk['refused'][] = ['e' => $one, 'missing' => $r['missing']];
        }
    }

    // WHAT THIS LETTER PROMISES THAT PAYROLL DOES NOT DO. The appointment letter
    // tells a new joiner that provident fund will be deducted in accordance with
    // the law, which is a normal clause and not the thing to change — this build
    // computes no PF, and until now nobody was told. A company putting that in
    // writing over a signature, above a payroll that does none of it, finds out
    // when the employee goes looking for the balance.
    //
    // A warning, never a gate: the letter is legitimate. The silence was the defect.
    $promises = [];

    if ($template !== null) {
        try {
            $promises = Letters::promisesNotKept($template, $structure->versionOn(date('Y-m-d')));
        } catch (\Throwable) {
            // No structure in force is already reported, loudly, by the payroll
            // screens. Repeating it here as a letter problem would send somebody
            // to the wrong screen.
            $promises = [];
        }
    }
?>
  <div class="page-header"><div><h2>Letters</h2></div>
<?php if ($preview !== null && ($preview['ok'] ?? false)): ?>
    <button class="btn btn-outline no-print" type="button" onclick="window.print()">
      <i class="fas fa-print"></i> Print or save as PDF</button>
<?php endif; ?>
  </div>
  <details class="why"><summary>Why a letter is a template, and why a blank is refused</summary>
    
    <p class="note">Seven templates in <code>config/letters.json</code> and one engine. A new letter
       type, or a change to the wording of an existing one, is an edit to that file &mdash; in
       SmartPRS&nbsp;2 it is a controller, and in most installations it is a Word file on somebody's
       desktop, so the version that goes out depends on whose desktop.</p>
    <p class="note"><b>A placeholder that resolves to nothing is refused, not left blank.</b> An
       appointment letter that goes out reading &ldquo;your annual cost to company will be&nbsp;
       &rdquo; is worse than one that failed to render: it is signed, filed and acted on, and
       nobody reads six familiar paragraphs closely enough to see the gap.</p>
  </details>

<?php foreach ($promises as $promise): ?>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="problem" style="margin:0"><b><?= e((string) $promise['scheme']) ?></b>:
      <?= e((string) $promise['why']) ?></div>
  </div>
<?php endforeach; ?>

  <div class="card">
    <form method="get">
      <input type="hidden" name="r" value="letters">
      <div class="row">
        <div style="flex:2"><label for="e">Employee</label>
<?php $letterChoices = ['all' => 'All employees (' . count(letterRecipients($store, $scope, $may('employee.letters.view'))) . ' active)']; foreach ($scope->only($store->all('employees'), $may('employee.letters.view')) as $row) {
    $letterChoices[(string) $row['id']] = trim((string) ($row['emp_code'] ?? '') . ' — ' . (string) ($row['name'] ?? ''), ' —');
} ?>
          <?= employeePicker('e', 'e', $letterChoices, $employeeId, '— type to search —') ?></div>
        <div style="flex:2"><label for="t">Letter</label>
          <select id="t" name="t">
