  <p class="note">Read-only: configuring a component needs
     <code>payroll.structure.publish</code>.</p>
<?php else: ?>
<?php if ($componentRulesInFiles): ?>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="problem" style="margin:0"><b>These rules are being kept in a file, not in
      MySQL.</b> The table <code>salary_component_rules</code> ships with this release and is not
      in this database yet, so the screen is using
      <code>storage/salary_component_rules.json</code> — the same file store the whole product
      falls back to when there is no database. It works, it is effective-dated the same way, and
      everything else on this installation is still in MySQL.
      <div class="note" style="margin-top:8px">The application cannot create the table itself: the
        account it runs as holds no schema privileges, which is deliberate and is what stops a
