         component, a calculation with its inputs missing, a percentage that is not an exact
         decimal, the same component twice for the same scope, or two components both claiming the
         balance. If any row is refused, <b>nothing</b> is published — a half-published set is
         neither the old rules nor the new ones. Publishing closes the rules in force on the day
         before and opens the new set, so a payslip reprinted for March still computes from March's
