  <?php // LOCKED READS AS LOCKED. The base stylesheet forces select/input to a
        // white background so a plain [disabled] attribute is nearly invisible —
        // this is the same opacity treatment the Payslip Format Designer already
        // uses for its own disabled buttons, scoped to this grid alone.
        //
        // ONE ROW, ALWAYS VISIBLE, NEVER WRAPPED — the owner's own correction
        // (10 Sep: "keep everything as previous - visible... single row format
        // only... minimum scrolling") ruled out the collapsed-summary design
        // this comment used to describe; buildRow() below always renders every
        // field. What this stylesheet controls is how WIDE each field is
        // allowed to get before that single row has to scroll sideways at all —
        // .cr-field used to be a fixed 112px regardless of screen width, which
        // is why adding Role (owner request, 18 Sep) made the row scroll
        // repeatedly even on a normal laptop screen. flex:1 1 <basis> instead
        // of flex:0 0 <basis> lets every field share whatever width the screen
        // actually has and only shrinks to the basis — the scroll floor — once
        // there truly isn't room, which is the "adjust... in a single view"
        // the owner asked for without reversing the no-wrap decision above it. ?>
  <style>
