  <details class="why"><summary>Why a batch is approved rather than imported</summary>
    <p class="note">Half the branches on SmartPRS&nbsp;2 have no device; attendance there is a
       supervisor's register mailed to HR at month end. This screen loads that register. <b>Upload
       writes nothing to attendance.</b> Every row is checked &mdash; who it names, whether the date
       is a date, whether the out time is after the in &mdash; and kept with its verdict. An
       administrator then approves the batch and each approved row becomes ordinary punches
       carrying <code>source=bulk</code> and the batch and line they came from, so approving the
       same batch twice writes nothing, and a rejected batch writes nothing at all.</p>
    <p class="note"><b>Three things SmartPRS&nbsp;2 did here that this refuses.</b> It matched a
       row by name when the code was missing and took whichever employee it saw last &mdash;
       here a name two employees share is refused naming both. It read <code>01/09/2026</code>
       with a library that accepts January &mdash; here the formats are declared and a value that
       does not read back as itself is refused. And it deleted a bad row on request &mdash; here a
       row is withdrawn and stays, so the file and the batch agree line for line.</p>
  </details>

