    <p class="note">The KPI catalogue &mdash; which KRA, which KPI, its description and how it is
       calculated &mdash; is <code>config/kra-kpi.json</code>, seeded from the collections/recovery
       industry's own KRA/KPI matrix. Pick who it applies to (a blank dropdown means <b>All</b>),
       tick <b>Keep</b> on every KPI that should count for that scope, and enter a target for the
       ones that already have one agreed &mdash; a KPI can be kept with no target yet. Only kept
       KPIs show up on KPI Achievements for an employee in this scope. Saving replaces the whole
       set kept for this exact scope: a target is never overwritten and unticking a KPI here is
       what stops it applying &mdash; saving closes whatever was open and opens new, dated rows for
       what is ticked, so an achievement recorded last month stays explained by last month's target
       even after this one changes. The most specific scope that covers an employee wins: a
       role-scoped setting beats a branch-scoped one beats a tenant-wide one.</p>
    <p class="note">A handful of KPIs here are marked <span class="badge badge-blue"><i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i> KPI name</span>
       &mdash; that means the matrix itself defines a companion figure (e.g. "Field Visits Completed")
       that is recorded in <b>Performance &amp; Rewards &rarr; KPI Achievements</b> against THIS
       target, and a percentage (e.g. "Visit Completion %") that is worked out automatically from
       the two, so it never appears here or in Performance as something to target or record on its
       own &mdash; recording it separately would just be a second, driftable copy of a number the
       system already computes.</p>
  </details>
