    <p class="note">A day the register refuses to pay needs a way out, or somebody edits the punch
       table. An approval adds a <b>new</b> punch carrying <code>source=regularised</code> and the id
       of the request — the device&rsquo;s own punch is never edited, so &ldquo;the reader missed the
       exit&rdquo; and &ldquo;the exit time was changed&rdquo; stay distinguishable when it is
       disputed. A rejection adds nothing at all: the day stays unsettled and keeps saying so,
       because a day that looks resolved and pays nothing is worse than one that admits it is
       unresolved.</p>
    <p class="note">It is two acts — requested, then decided — so the person who benefits from a
       corrected time is not the person who approves it. This build has one role that can do both,
       which is a <b>stated</b> ceiling rather than a silent one.</p>
