    <p class="note">All of it from <code>config/calendar.json</code>. A six-day week, a night shift
       and Diwali are not code. The <b>proration basis</b> is declared rather than defaulted,
       because prorating over calendar days and over working days give different payslips for the
       same month and the same attendance — a platform that picks one silently has made a business
       decision on the customer&rsquo;s behalf and not told them.</p>
  </div>

<?php
  // WHEN THIS EMPLOYMENT EXISTED. `employees` carries a joining date and NO exit
  // date — leaving is a `status` flag — so nothing on this screen could have
  // told a month somebody worked from a month after they left. That is the
  // defect Platform\Lifecycle\EmploymentTimeline names in its own docblock, and
  // it is why the figure above can be zero with a reason beside it.
  $lifecycle = $timeline->events(Employment::code($employment));
  $exited = $timeline->exitedOn(Employment::code($employment));
?>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Employee timeline
      <span class="note">joined, confirmed, moved, left &mdash; as dated events</span></h2>
<?php if ($lifecycle === []): ?>
    <div class="empty" style="padding:18px"><i class="fas fa-timeline"></i>Nothing recorded. This
      employee is paid normally &mdash; an empty timeline answers <b>nothing</b>, not
      &ldquo;not employed&rdquo;, because most ported employees have no events yet and reading
      silence as an answer would stop every payslip in the tenant.</div>
<?php else: ?>
    <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Effective</th><th>Event</th><th>Reason</th><th>Recorded by</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
<?php foreach ($lifecycle as $event): ?>
      <tr>
        <td><?= e((string) $event['effective_on']) ?></td>
        <td><span class="badge badge-<?= (string) $event['kind'] === 'exited' ? 'red' : 'gray' ?>"><?=
          e($timeline->kinds()[(string) $event['kind']] ?? (string) $event['kind']) ?></span></td>
        <td class="note"><?= e((string) ($event['reason'] ?? '')) ?></td>
        <td class="note"><?= e((string) ($event['recorded_by'] ?? '')) ?></td>
      </tr>
<?php endforeach; ?>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
<?php endif; ?>
<?php if ($exited !== null): ?>
    <div class="problem" style="margin:14px 0 0"><b>Exited on <?= e($exited) ?>.</b> No month
      beginning after that date is payable, whatever the punches say &mdash; a device that keeps
      sending, a row imported twice or a badge somebody else is using does not know that this
      person left, and a payslip for a month after somebody leaves is what this product was rebuilt
      to stop.</div>
<?php endif; ?>
